40,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some interesting stuff! Transport costs vary a lot depending on the distance, and those whole-building lets have strict non-refundable deposits. We need to be careful about how we handle late cancellations!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"That is a very important point, Mio. I have found that our past attendance was quite low, and some members left the club entirely. We must choose a place that truly encourages everyone to join.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings are concerning. Publicly run centers require a tedious lottery process and an incredibly rigid application. Furthermore, self-catering is a significant drain on the organizers' time. We must avoid options that demand excessive paperwork or cooking duties.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that some inland places cram eight people into one room! That sounds like a nightmare. If we're all squeezed in like sardines, nobody will get any real rest, and we'll be exhausted!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The club hall is too crowded for a continuous block, and many members can't arrive early without overnight stays. We must consider the actual cost of these accommodations to avoid any further financial strain.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Mio,,"If transport is such a huge part of the budget, maybe staying closer is better? Also, those non-refundable deposits are scary! We should figure out a fair way to handle it if someone cancels.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"Perhaps a place where we all share a common living space would be best. If we can find a way to encourage the different year-groups to mingle in the evenings, it might revitalize the club's spirit.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If we prioritize a common space, we must ensure it doesn't come with a requirement for us to manage the meals. A place with professional catering would be far more reasonable for the organizers.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Exactly! If we're too tired, we can't mingle or train. We need a place with actual beds and enough space to breathe, not some crowded hall where we'll be grumpy and sleepy!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"Professional catering and better beds sound ideal, but they increase the price. We cannot afford to guess the budget this time. Any option we choose must have a fixed, transparent cost to prevent further deficits.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I agree with Misaki! Transparency is key. If we go for a place with catering and better beds, we just have to make sure the flat fee covers it all without leaving anyone out of pocket.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is a delicate balance, isn't it? While costs are vital, we must remember that the heart of this camp is the people. A place that fosters warmth and friendship is worth every penny.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Warmth and friendship are fine, but they shouldn't be built on the backs of a few exhausted organizers. We must prioritize a destination that offers a turnkey service to avoid burnout and administrative chaos.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if the organizers are the only ones who aren't exhausted, it's still a fail! We need a place where everyone—including the organizers—can actually sleep! Let's not pick anywhere that crowds us together!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"We cannot prioritize comfort or convenience if the cost is unpredictable. If we choose a high-end option without a guaranteed fixed price, we risk another deficit that the club simply cannot sustain.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I totally get it! Let's look for a spot that's close enough to keep transport cheap, but has a clear, fixed price for everything. That way, it's fair for everyone and no one gets a surprise bill!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree. Let us seek a place that is affordable and organized, yet cozy enough to bring our members together. A warm atmosphere will surely encourage those who have been hesitant to join us.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree, provided that ""organized"" means the facility handles the logistics. We must explicitly reject any option involving a lottery system or self-catering. The organizers' time is a finite resource that we cannot afford to waste.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm with you! No lotteries and no sardine-rooms! Let's pick a place where we can actually sleep and wake up feeling great, or we'll just be grumpy the whole time!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I will support any option that provides a guaranteed, all-inclusive price. We must prioritize financial stability over convenience or luxury to ensure the club's accounts remain solvent. Let's be cautious with our final choice.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
